A||||14||fiero56||Radar Detectors||||5||
Z||000000||fiero56||10-06-2000||10:02 PM||||I was surfing through ebay today, and decided to see what radar detectors typically go for on ebay. I was amazed to see how many are for sale on there, and at how cheap they appear to be going for. What is the reason these detectors go for so cheap? Appears many sellers are actually vendors, selling through e-bay. I nopticed several great deals, that expire within the next 10 hours, and most didn't even have any bids. What's going on? Is there something I am not aware of about buying detectors over ebay? Too many vendors, not enough buyers? I might just bid on one of these babies tonight. I have never really felt the need for one, but lately the cops around here seem to have something stuck up their butts, that just won't go away. Plus, my highway travel will start to increase, and just figured it would be nice to have a new toy <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>Why are the prices so low, and no bids?||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||10-06-2000||10:05 PM||||I love it when I pull over people, walk up to their car, and their radar detector is flashing and beeping at its maximum rate, and the person looks at me and says..."did I do something wrong officer?"....<P>MMMWAAAAAAHHH! ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Formula||10-06-2000||10:14 PM||||I have the new whistler top o' the line and it works GREAT in west virginia, but for some reason it doesnt work in pennsylvania... it doesnt make sense||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||10-06-2000||10:43 PM||||I was with a friend once when he got pulled over. He left his detector on the windshield, and wouldn't take it off, he said the suction cup marks are a pain to get off, and don't work as well the second time he puts them on. The cop just looked at the detector and I knew it wasn't going to go well...this was in Columbus...very interesting portion of my life...first time I have ever been accused of smuggling pot, by a cop even...<BR>I lost some respect for cops then(no offence My7Fieros), and at other times. Now I don't really care about them as long as they leave me alone...they haven't lately.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||10-06-2000||10:51 PM||||fiero56, I think its that there are too many vendors and not enough buyers. I'm not sure about other states, but in my state of MD, they are legal, but in VA they are not.  It limits the market.  Also I have heard that most radar detectors don't do much compared to the Valentine One.  Everyone I have ever talked to about Radar Detectors talks about how great it is.  However it 400 bucks.  I don't think I am going to get one unless its the V1, but I need 400 spare bucks first...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||10-06-2000||11:03 PM||||Just noticed something which I should have figured out without having to look.  <P>I went to check it out on ebay.  If you read the extremely long, web paged style auctions, it says they are "Refurbished".  I noticed this too when I was looking for CD-RW drives.  Yeah they were cheap, but they were all refurbs.     ||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||10-06-2000||11:46 PM||||I noticed most ads said "refurbished", but there are a few that say "brand new, not refurbished." I also have heard great things about the V1, but a ticket is cheaper than spending $400 on a detector, and still leaving open possibility for ticket. My main concern was why the low prices. Sounds like not enough demand to justify supply(sounds like the oil situation, only in reverse, doesn't it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).||||reg||1
Z||000007||olympic||10-07-2000||02:03 AM||||  Detectors are cheap even new!  I see refurbs for sale in stores for under $50 all the time.  Even brand new the prices have really come down, just like any electronics.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||10-07-2000||06:28 AM||||There's nothing necessarily wrong with a refurbished anything.  My brother in law (computer college student) recently bought a refurbished laptop from Gateway (sorry, GT Bastard).  It's close to the top of the line and he hasn't had any problems with it so far.  Same warranty, etc.  <P>As for the thought that a speeding ticket costs less than a $400 radar detector...I'd say it all depends on age, speed, etc.  If I got a ticket for going 10 over, I wouldn't blink an eye.  On the other hand, what if you got a ticket for 20 over.  I'm 32 and married with no current tickets (not saying that you have any).  Someone who is alot younger, single with some other tickets on thier record could find their insurance rates getting higher.  <P>Just a thought.  I've never had one and never will (no need--I rarely go out of town anyway).  Valentine One is supposed to be the best, but there are a lot of good (and cheaper) detectors out there.  <P>I'm trying to figure out what my point was.  It's early and I had some time to kill before going to the torture chamber (er...I mean, work) so I thought I'd log on and see what everyone was up to.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||10-07-2000||11:11 AM||||To further confuse the issue...<BR>A lot of the larger departments have added laser to their tool kits. <BR>Because laser doesn't scatter like radar does, it's much more difficult to detect. Usually by the time it's detected, you're already tagged.<BR>Does the V-1 detect laser? Been a long time since I read any tests.<BR>I haven't used a radar detector in about 5 years. <BR>When I'm on the open interstate, I usually drive about 10 over. Maybe just a bit more depending on traffic. I find that if there are at least some people passing me, then I'm usually safe. <BR>When I drive through little towns, I obey the speed limit, carefully. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (soon to receive transplant.)<BR>88 "pretzeled" Formula <P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000010||hugh||10-07-2000||02:43 PM||||I don't remember why,but the courts in New Jersey have ruled against the use of Laser by the police(about 2 years ago).||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||10-07-2000||03:32 PM||||I've pretty much given up on radar/laser detectors. More annoying than usefull. Both my bosses are ex cops. we've talked about how both radar and laser work. I've done a bunch of diggin on top of that.<P>Radar detectors only work if the radar is on. Most of the ones who are really shooting it at you leave it off until you are inside range and they are sure they have you. <P>Another trick is to use a radar detector to find areas that have things that cause false alarms. They set up in that area to nail the people who assume the area is just falsing them.<P>Laser units I've seen are all hand held jobs and are all manual triggered. If your detector goes off they have you or someone right by you. The laser only needs a second or so of activation to clock. The odds of you picking up the pulse with a detector are extreamly bad.<P>Newer lasers are in developement that have even thighter beams. It will be even eisier to shoot single car in a crowd with them.||||reg||1
Z||000012||BroCar 87||10-07-2000||08:40 PM||||AHHH   How bout radar/laser JAMMERS!!!! Now those are sweeeet! Most likely illegal, but sweeet!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature2.jpg"> <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||6
Z||000013||theogre||10-07-2000||09:26 PM||||Jamming devices for any type radio are banned by the FCC. That includes anti radar units. They like to lock people up for those. <P>On the other hand a number of years ago the cops in some places tried stuffing devices to false trip the detectors behind guard rails and such. The FCC made them stop.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||10-07-2000||09:37 PM||||In the days before cellphones, I worked for a company that used to lease UHF IMTS (stone age) mobile phones. These suckers put out 30 watts at 450 MHZ. Used to set off Fuzzbusters for blocks around. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (soon to receive transplant.)<BR>88 "pretzeled" Formula <P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
